/F1 12 Tf
16 TL
50 750 Td
/F1 18 Tf (OpsPulse Incident Runbook: PostgreSQL Connection Pool Saturation) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
/F1 14 Tf (1. Incident Description & Scope) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
(Symptoms: Microservices throw database connection errors. API latency spikes to 10+ seconds.) Tj T*
(Log Pattern: FATAL: remaining connection slots are reserved for non-replication superuser connections) Tj T*
(Secondary Pattern: org.postgresql.util.PSQLException: FATAL: sorry, too many clients already) Tj T*
(Affected Components: PostgreSQL cluster, PgBouncer pooler, Auth Service, Checkout Service.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf (2. Root Cause Diagnostics Protocol) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
(Step 1: Inspect connection counts by application state in PostgreSQL:) Tj T*
(  SELECT count\(*\), state, usename FROM pg_stat_activity GROUP BY state, usename;) Tj T*
(Step 2: Detect long-running queries holding locks and starving connection pools:) Tj T*
(  SELECT pid, client_addr, now\(\) - query_start AS duration, state, query FROM pg_stat_activity) Tj T*
(  WHERE state != idle AND now\(\) - query_start > interval 30 seconds ORDER BY duration DESC LIMIT 10;) Tj T*
(Step 3: Identify blocking locks and blocked transactions:) Tj T*
(  SELECT blocked_locks.pid AS blocked_pid, blocking_locks.pid AS blocking_pid, blocking_activity.query) Tj T*
(  FROM pg_catalog.pg_locks blocked_locks) Tj T*
(  JOIN pg_catalog.pg_locks blocking_locks ON blocking_locks.locktype = blocked_locks.locktype;) Tj T*
T*
/F1 14 Tf (3. Emergency Remediation & Fix Actions) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
(Action A \(Terminate Runaway Transactions\): Kill blocking PID immediately:) Tj T*
(  SELECT pg_terminate_backend\(blocking_pid\) FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE pid = <blocking_pid>;) Tj T*
(Action B \(Enforce Idle Transaction Timeout\): Disconnect leaked idle connections automatically:) Tj T*
(  ALTER DATABASE production_db SET idle_in_transaction_session_timeout = 20000;) Tj T*
(Action C \(PgBouncer Configuration Tuning\):) Tj T*
(  Ensure max_client_conn is 1000 and default_pool_size is adjusted to avoid backend saturation.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
